  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`, but I haven't run the tests or added a test for it.\n\nFor an open bound, the method moved the value the wrong way, using `bound - dir` instead of `bound + dir`. With `min_open=True`, a value below the range was clamped to `min - 1`, which is outside the range. For example, `IntRange(0, 10, min_open=True, clamp=True)` returned `-1` for the input `-5`. It now returns `1`. The same swap affected `max_open`, which returned `max + 1` instead of `max - 1`.\n\nClosed bounds were already correct.",
